The '''2026 Isle of Wight Council election''' took place on 7 May 2026 to elect members to [[Isle of Wight Council]] on the [[Isle of Wight]], [[England]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 January 2023 |title=Election timetable in England |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/election-timetable-in-england/election-timetable-in-england#district-councils2 |access-date=4 September 2024 |publisher=[[Electoral Commission (UK)|Electoral Commission]]}}</ref> 39 seats were elected. This was on the same day as other [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|local elections]]. The council remained under [[no overall control]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-05-08 |title=Isle of Wight election result - Local Elections 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2026/england/councils/E06000046 |access-date=2026-05-08 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

== Background ==
At the [[2021 Isle of Wight Council election|2021 election]], the Conservatives lost the council to [[no overall control]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Isle of Wight result - Local Elections 2021 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/election/2021/england/councils/E06000046 |access-date=2024-11-29 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> There are plans for the council to move to a committee system in 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Isle of Wight Council to move to committee system in 2025 |url=https://www.iow.gov.uk/news/isle-of-wight-council-to-move-to-committee-system-in-2025/ |access-date=2024-11-29 |website=Isle of Wight Council |language=en}}</ref>

