===Changes===
*October 2022: Steve Hastings (Conservative) resigns – by-election held November 2022<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hill |first1=Louise |title=Former leader of Isle of Wight Conservative councillors resigns: ‘I no longer believe in the Conservative Party’ (updated) |url=https://onthewight.com/former-leader-of-isle-of-wight-conservative-councillors-resigns-i-no-longer-believe-in-the-conservative-party/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=On the Wight |date=10 October 2022}}</ref>
*November 2022: Nick Stuart (Liberal Democrats) gains by-election from Conservatives<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Brighstone, Calbourne and Shalfleet Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21385/#2022-11-24 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
*May 2023: Michael Lilley (Independent) joins Liberal Democrats<ref>{{cite news |last1=Perry |first1=Sally |title=Isle of Wight power shift: Cllr Michael Lilley bids farewell to Alliance Group (updated) |url=https://onthewight.com/isle-of-wight-power-shift-cllr-michael-lilley-bids-farewell-to-alliance-group/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=On the Wight |date=9 May 2023}}</ref>
*July 2023: Daryll Pitcher (Vectis) resigns – by-election held August 2023<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hill |first1=Louise |title=Councillor Daryll Pitcher resigns months after rape conviction |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-hampshire-66193247 |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=BBC News |date=13 July 2023}}</ref>
*August 2023: Sarah Redrup (Liberal Democrats) gains by-election from Vectis<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Wootton Bridge Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21419/#2023-08-24 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
*October 2023: Gary Peace (Conservative) resigns – by-election held December 2023<ref>{{cite news |last1=Perry |first1=Sally |title=Conservative Isle of Wight councillor resigns, forcing another by-election (update 2) |url=https://onthewight.com/conservative-isle-of-wight-councillor-resigns-forcing-another-by-election/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=On the Wight |date=23 October 2023}}</ref>
*December 2023: Ed Blake (Conservative) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Ventnor and St Lawrence Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21418/#2023-12-21 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
*March 2025: Suzie Ellis (Conservative), John Medland (Independent) and Tig Outlaw (Conservative) resign – by-elections held May 2025<ref>{{cite news |last1=Perry |first1=Sally |title=Isle of Wight elections: Central Rural to elect new councillor on 1st May |url=https://onthewight.com/isle-of-wight-elections-central-rural-to-elect-new-councillor-on-1st-may/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=On the Wight |date=6 March 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Perry |first1=Sally |title=Is your Isle of Wight councillor planning to stand down for a May by-election or carry on until 2026? |url=https://onthewight.com/is-your-isle-of-wight-councillor-planning-to-stand-down-for-a-may-by-election-or-carry-on-until-2026/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=On the Wight |date=21 March 2025}}</ref>
*May 2025: Caroline Gladwin (Reform) and David Maclean (Reform) gain by-elections from Conservatives; Becca Cameron (Independent) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Freshwater South Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21396/#2025-05-01 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Central Rural Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21387/#2025-05-01 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Lake North Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21398/#2025-05-01 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
*June 2025: Rodney Downer (Independent) resigns – by-election held July 2025<ref>{{cite news |last1=Moreno |first1=Jon |title="I'm just an ordinary bloke" says retired Rodney Downer reflecting on council career |url=https://www.countypress.co.uk/news/25217543.isle-wight-man-rodney-downer-looks-back-council-career/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=Isle of Wight County Press |date=6 June 2025 |language=en}}</ref>
*July 2025: Mark Jefferies (Independent Network) gains by-election from independent<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Wroxall, Lowtherville and Bonchurch Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21420/#2025-07-10 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
