**David Maclean (Reform) resigns – by-election held October 2025<ref>{{cite news |title=Isle of Wight Reform UK councillor resigns after four months |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4glqvldl3zo |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=BBC News |date=20 August 2025}}</ref>
**Clare Mosdell (Conservative) leaves party to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Pickles |first1=Rufus |title=Former leader of County Hall Conservatives resigns from group |url=https://www.countypress.co.uk/news/25390237.isle-wight-councillor-resigns-conservative-group/ |access-date=30 January 2026 |work=Isle of Wight County Press |date=14 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref>
*October 2025:
**Bill Nigh (Reform) wins by-election<ref>{{cite web |title=Local Elections Archive Project — Lake North Ward |url=https://www.andrewteale.me.uk/leap/ward/21398/#2025-10-02 |website=www.andrewteale.me.uk |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>
**Our Island dissolved – Jonathan Bacon sits as an independent<ref>{{cite web |title=Our Island [De-registered 15/10/25] |url=https://search.electoralcommission.org.uk/English/Registrations/PP12513 |website=Electoral Commission |access-date=30 January 2026}}</ref>

